<title>UK: EU raises medium quality wheat import duty.</title>
<headline>EU raises medium quality wheat import duty.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will raise duties on transatlantic imports of medium quality soft wheat on Wednesday to 53.04 Ecus per tonne from 46.46 Ecus, European Commission figures showed.  </p>
<p>Import duties on other grain varieties will remain unchanged.</p>
<p>New barley and rye marketing years started on July 1 but the sorghum season starts on October 1.</p>
</text>
